From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: refresh the tx agg session timer under NPU offload

On boards using Airoha NPU offload, TX block-ack sessions get torn down mid-transfer 
whenever the peer negotiates a BlockAck timeout (Intel stations commonly do). Offloaded 
traffic bypasses mac80211, so nothing refreshes the session timer — the driver only did 
that for WED devices, and the NPU path was gated out. The result is a DELBA in the middle 
of a transfer and throughput collapsing to un-aggregated rates, with no recovery until 
unrelated traffic happens to take the software path. Extending the gate to cover NPU 
devices keeps the session alive the same way it already works on WED.

Signed-off-by: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1511,7 +1511,8 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) && wcid->sta) {
+	if ((mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed) ||
+	     mt76_npu_device_active(&dev->mt76)) && wcid->sta) {
 		struct ieee80211_sta *sta;
 		u8 tid;
 
